pull_request.body:
## Summary

Adds a bounded developer-machine self-update path for the installed Chat Agent Platform without changing the six-tool Chat authority surface.

The intended user-facing UX remains one action in the existing tray:

`Дополнительно -> Обновить`

One click checks accepted `BogdanAIP/chat-agent-platform/main`. If the installed accepted-main SHA is current, no bootstrap runs. If a newer accepted fast-forward `main` exists, the updater installs it through the canonical bootstrap. There is no separate check button, updater window, confirmation dialog, or updater desktop shortcut.

## Current identity

- BASE: `0223aa3f5e8a800c4e9eb61ec88e6703450fa9e0` — current accepted `main`
- HEAD: `bd7e65967eb02119125869e8f70e4e619e627323`
- branch: `chat/main-self-update`
- state: Draft; **not ready to merge**

The branch is current with accepted `main`. PR #149 is merged and no longer part of #150's pending acceptance.

## Stage Research boundary

Decision remains **NARROW** (`project-context/MAIN_SELF_UPDATE_RESEARCH.md`).

Selected boundary:

- fixed source: `BogdanAIP/chat-agent-platform` `main` only;
- private bare cache under `%LOCALAPPDATA%\ChatAgentPlatform\update-cache`;
- atomic fetch of exact `main`;
- detached clean exact-target worktree;
- known installed SHA must be an ancestor of target, otherwise fail closed;
- one named updater mutex;
- `bootstrap-chat-platform.ps1` remains the only installer;
- installed-main receipt is published only from clean exact official `origin/main` after successful bootstrap;
- tray updater shares the existing lifecycle-busy projection so platform lifecycle and update cannot race.

## Post-#149 continuity finding

Refreshing #150 onto the newly accepted `main` exposed a real updater-continuity gap in the earlier design and invalidated the old physical acceptance as final evidence.

Before #150 itself is merged, accepted `main@e810b9dd...` does not contain `chat-platform-tray-update.ps1` or the updater integration. The earlier updater would fetch an accepted newer `main` and immediately run that target's bootstrap. A target that predates the updater could therefore overwrite the installed tray/runtime with a version that no longer contains the updater. The still-running old tray could report the update as successful, so an immediate second click did not prove that the updater survived a tray/process restart.

This is consistent with the reported local machine not matching the intended persistent one-click updater UX.

## Current continuity fix

Current HEAD adds a fail-closed target self-update contract before any target bootstrap is invoked.

A candidate target must contain and bind the updater path across:

- `scripts/bootstrap-chat-platform.ps1`;
- `scripts/chat-platform-tray.ps1`;
- `scripts/chat-platform-tray-update.ps1`;
- `scripts/chat-platform-update-core.ps1`;
- `scripts/chat-platform-update.ps1`.

Required integration markers include bootstrap shipping of updater assets, tray registration through `Register-CapUpdateTrayMenu`, fixed official-main update mechanics, result handoff, and the one-click Update action.

If the target does not preserve that contract, the updater stops **before target bootstrap**, records `status=blocked` with `reason=target_missing_self_update_contract`, and the tray reports that the available `main` does not yet contain the built-in updater and that nothing was changed.

This deliberately means a development-installed #150 updater must refuse to downgrade itself into the current pre-#150 accepted `main`. Once #150 is accepted into `main`, later accepted-main updates naturally carry the updater contract forward.


## Independent-review remediation

A genuinely fresh independent semantic review on 2026-09-11 found one surviving P3 on prior HEAD `607a301b23c3543c47778038b605f6a5ce4d700b`: the updater invoked the canonical bootstrap while the installed platform/tunnel could still be running. If a future accepted `main` changed the pinned `tunnel-client.exe` bytes, the bootstrap would deterministically fail at the tunnel install guard before the intended running -> updated -> running continuity could complete.

Current HEAD closes that finding:

- the updater snapshots whether persistent desired state was `running`;
- after target continuity validation and immediately before bootstrap, it invokes the installed manager `Stop` path and waits for it to complete;
- only then can target bootstrap replace/update tunnel/runtime bytes;
- if any later update step fails after the stop attempt, the error path attempts to restart the installed manager when the pre-update desired state was `running`;
- successful restart state is reflected in the terminal result;
- the target self-update contract now requires the quiesce/recovery markers, so a later accepted target cannot silently drop this safety property;
- `tests/test_chat_platform_update.py` contains a structural regression asserting continuity-gate -> Stop -> bootstrap ordering and recovery Start on the error path;
- a Windows behavioral regression uses an isolated local Git fixture and an ephemeral test-only updater copy to prove `Stop -> Bootstrap -> Start` on forced post-stop bootstrap failure, restoration of prior `running` intent, and preservation of the previous installed SHA without a false target receipt. Production source authority remains fixed to official GitHub `main`;
- follow-up internal review also closed three adjacent fail-closed gaps: malformed persisted desired state is rejected before quiesce, a process that never acquires the updater mutex cannot mutate the active owner's shared state/result, and tray terminal results are bound to the exact child PID/action/completion time so stale or foreign result files cannot be mistaken for the current click.

Because this changes the consequence-bearing physical update path, all target-Windows physical evidence from `607a301b...` is now development history only and must be requalified on the exact current HEAD before merge.

## Files

- `scripts/chat-platform-update-core.ps1` — Git/source/state primitives.
- `scripts/chat-platform-update.ps1` — fixed-source Check/Update wrapper plus target continuity gate.
- `scripts/chat-platform-tray-update.ps1` — one-click tray adapter and reason-specific terminal notifications.
- `scripts/chat-platform-tray.ps1` — `Дополнительно -> Обновить` registration and lifecycle integration.
- `scripts/bootstrap-chat-platform.ps1` — ships updater assets and records successful exact-main install identity.
- `tests/test_chat_platform_update.py` — source/tray/continuity contracts plus local-Git update behavior.
- `project-context/MAIN_SELF_UPDATE_RESEARCH.md` — narrow research brief.

## Evidence status

Historical physical evidence on `4d83e542...` is stale.

Exact HEAD `607a301b...` later passed the development install, visible tray UX, fail-closed pre-#150-main continuity check, byte-preservation check and full tray-process restart. That evidence proved the updater survived a blocked downgrade into pre-#150 `main`.

The independent-review remediation and subsequent fail-closed hardening change the consequence-bearing updater/tray path, so `607a301b...` physical evidence is **STALE for final acceptance** on current HEAD `bd7e65967eb02119125869e8f70e4e619e627323`.

Exact final HEAD `bd7e65967eb02119125869e8f70e4e619e627323` now passes the full hosted workflow set: `ci`, CodeQL Security, Secret History Scan, Chat Profile Acceptance, Semantic Projection Acceptance, and Stage 26.3B Windows Application L3 Acceptance. The Windows unit/contract suite includes the quiesce/recovery behavior, duplicate-updater ownership isolation, desired-state fail-closed checks, and tray terminal-result correlation.

## Remaining work before merge

1. install exact HEAD `bd7e65967eb02119125869e8f70e4e619e627323` on the target Windows machine and requalify the visible tray UX plus fail-closed pre-#150-main continuity across a full tray restart;
2. physically verify the installed runtime remains coherent around the new pre-bootstrap quiesce/recovery boundary; hosted Windows behavioral fixtures cover the otherwise-unreachable pre-merge transition against a self-update-capable target;
3. run a genuinely fresh independent semantic review on the exact final BASE..HEAD after physical evidence is current;
4. only then resolve final identity/evidence and consider Ready/merge.

#150 remains Draft until exact-head physical evidence and the fresh independent review are current.
